@startuml turn-queue-sequence
' SPEC: _spec/apps/ui/starchess/turn-queue-sequence.puml
' purpose: Simultaneous turn queue — planning Q:<w>;<b>, End submits, B < C < F then w then b, next snap.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Simultaneous Turn Queue

actor Player as P
participant "apps/ui StarChess screen" as UI <<app>>
participant "endScTurn" as ES <<app>>
participant "resolveTurn" as RT <<app>>
participant "scOutcome" as OUT <<app>>
database "ScFenSnapshot" as FEN <<db>>

== Turn open ==

UI ARROW_MAIN ES : ""beginScTurn(snapshot)""\n(fog-visible legal king-checks)
note right of ES
  Checks resolve **before** intent.
  Breaking contact later still paid the
  **parting shot** at turn open.
  Live End passes ""skipTurnStartChecks"".
  Atomic replay / tests may still run
  checks inside ""endScTurn"" (default).
end note

== Planning ==

P ARROW_MAIN UI : queue special + classical for own side
UI ARROW_MAIN FEN : ""Q:<sideQueue>;<sideQueue>""\n(B/F then C, or C then B/F)
P ARROW_MAIN UI : End / timeout submits
UI ARROW_MAIN ES : ""endScTurn(snapshot)""

== Resolve ==

ES ARROW_MAIN ES : resolve rank-major: B → C → F\n(+ king-checks unless skipped)\nw then b within each rank

group 1 · turn-open legal king-checks (when not skipped)
  ES ARROW_MAIN ES : white, then black\n""applyPendingKingShots"" + ""collectLegalKingChecks""
  ES ARROW_ERROR ES : adjacent kings — **mutual** chip, **1 HP per checker**\n(a king left at 0 HP bails — no B/C/F)
end

group 2 · rank B (specials before combat)
  ES ARROW_MAIN ES : white B, then black B\n(applySpecial: spawn / mine / warp / siege)
end

group 3 · rank C (classical, both sides on same board)
  ES ARROW_MAIN RT : resolveTurn(white, black)
  RT ARROW_MAIN RT : attacks — visible targets (start board)\n(attack → death → occupy)
  RT ARROW_MAIN RT : moves — occupy, move collisions, mine triggers
  RT ARROW_MAIN RT : path-reveal fog approaches — ""pathRevealFrom"" →\ndiscovery square; fired only — fizzle unless attacker\nstill on ""pathRevealFrom"" and ""to"" holds the\nexact in-the-way victim
end

group 4 · rank F (specials after combat)
  ES ARROW_MAIN ES : white F, then black F\n(applySpecial: post-move siege / late drops)
end

== Next snap ==

ES ARROW_MAIN FEN : new snapshot (turn+1, ""G:"" refilled to income)
ES ARROW_ERROR FEN : phase ""O"" when either ""kingLives"" side hits 0
FEN ARROW_OPTIONAL OUT : " ""scOutcome(snap)"" "
FEN ARROW_QUEUE UI : cumulative fog for both sides (""vision.ts"")

note over ES
  Gas does not accumulate; ""endScTurn"" refills to full income
  next turn (income == turn tier 1 / 2 / 3).
end note

note over OUT
  **Terminal outcome, derived from HP.** ""scOutcome(snap)"" reads
  ""kingLives"" only: both at 0 → **draw**, exactly one at 0 → the other
  side wins, otherwise ""null"". No persisted winner field, no SCFEN
  grammar change.
  A draw is reachable because **adjacent kings chip each other
  simultaneously** — the shot is not gated on the shooter's own HP, so a
  king that dies in the pass still returns fire and equal HP ends 0/0
  (see resolve.puml). Phase ""O"" is **absorbing**: ""endScTurn"" throws on
  a non-""P"" snapshot, so no further turn can be resolved.
end note

note over RT
  **Three phases.** 1) attacks on targets visible at resolve start (start
  board); 2) moves + collisions for phase-1 survivors; 3) path-reveal fog
  approaches fire **after** moves — fizzle (dropped) unless the attacker
  still occupies ""pathRevealFrom"" (survived phases 1–2, origin not
  re-occupied by a phase-2 mover, not sieged — rooks never relocate) and
  ""to"" holds the exact in-the-way victim ""a.victim"" (empty, converging
  same-side ally, or a different non-in-the-way enemy → fizzle, no
  capture). ""applyPathRevealAttack"" is the shared source of truth for the
  board-state fizzles; siege + origin-re-occupation gates are pre-filtered
  by the engine loop, so ""pathRevealAttacks"" holds
  **only attacks that fired**. A target still fogged at contact becomes a
  move-phase collision (capture/occupy, no attack cue). Snapshots:
  ""afterMove"" (post-phase-2) and ""afterAll"" (post-phase-3).
end note
@enduml
